# ============================================================================
# VIOLET CITY, expanded  (28x24 blocks, buffer 1020/1300; vanilla 20x18)
# Source: buildviolet.py -> violet_base.amap; this file = rough.py --seed 2 --p 0.45
#   then violet_meta.py adds this header and violet_objs.txt
# ============================================================================
# KEPT: vanilla rows 0-8, cols 4-18 are pasted verbatim at cols 6-20: Sprout
#   Tower between its two moat ponds, the tower approach and sign, the Gym
#   (W) and Earl's Academy (E) flanking it, the cemetery house by the west
#   moat, the Surf-only Rare Candy nook NE. Also kept: Route 36 leaves W on
#   row 4, the nickname house stays at the same coords (3,15), the rock
#   outcrop (70 6b/72 6d) at the W edge, the Center + Route 31 gate (0e) on
#   the E edge, Route 32 S, the south fruit tree, PP Up NW.
# ADDED (cf. pokefollow Viridian: denser, a second street):
#   Main street (row 9) runs the full width; a N-S avenue from the tower to
#     Route 32 crosses it and a second street (row 14).
#   Old-houses quarter W, S and NE: seven 2c-2f houses (tea house, elders,
#     the Kimono Girls' dresser...); Kyle's house moves to the second street.
#   A Mart (18 19/16 17) next to the Center.
#   Garden pond SW with flower beds and the fruit tree.
#   Earl's practice field SE: fenced tall grass where Academy students
#     battle and wild Pokemon live; Earl coaches here.
# CONNECTIONS: W row 4 (steps 8-9) -> Route 36 (offset); S cols 13-14 ->
#   Route 32 (was col 7: offset); E gate warps move from (39,24/25) to
#   (55,24/25). Every interior warp back into Violet needs new coords.
# ============================================================================
ref VioletCity
key .=01 ,=02 "=03 *=04 T=05 G=0e 1=14 2=15 m=16 n=17 a=18 b=19 g=1a h=1b c=2c d=2d e=2e f=2f ~=35 s=45 S=47 q=48 w=49 p=4a (=54 )=55 [=58 ]=59 #=61 U=65 R=6b V=6d r=70 v=72 ^=76 A=1c B=1d C=1e D=1f E=22 F=23 H=26 I=27 J=28 K=29 L=2a M=3c N=5d O=60 P=74 Q=75 W=79
key !=3c ?=3d @=3e $=3f &=64 +=62 |=60 <=5d >=5e %=61 /=5c
